> so why not selvla?
>

I feel like selvla is settling.  I'll take it if nothing better comes up,
but you can define things that aren't words.  You can define concepts (which
are, I admit are typically expressed in words) and symbols, too.


> I think to define is to specify the meaning, but I don't know how to
> say "specify". We have "specific", but not "specify". We also have "ca'e",
> but it doesn't have a rafsi. "ca'esmu" is glossed as
> "push-ing-meaning(s)??".


Seems a tad too figurative...  As I understand, {ca'e} the discursive and
{-ca'e-} the rafsi aren't related.

-- 
          Alex R

